    <item>
      <title>Work by Seok-Jun Chang featured on the MPA webpage</title>
      <link>http://asgard-ari.github.io/post/2026-05-08-seok-jun-work-featured-on-mpa/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 08 May 2026 12:00:00 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>http://asgard-ari.github.io/post/2026-05-08-seok-jun-work-featured-on-mpa/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Work by former group member Seok-Jun Chang has been featured on the Max Planck Institute for Astrophysics (MPA) website:
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.mpa-garching.mpg.de/1147117/hl202605&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;https://www.mpa-garching.mpg.de/1147117/hl202605&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The MPA highlight, titled &amp;ldquo;Radiative Transfer Shapes Hydrogen Lines in Little Red Dots&amp;rdquo;, presents results on how resonance, Raman, and Thomson scattering shape hydrogen emission lines in Little Red Dots and discusses the implications for interpreting these systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The featured work is based on the paper by Seok-Jun Chang, Max Gronke, Jorryt Matthee, and Charlotte Mason on hydrogen line formation in Little Red Dots.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Links to paper:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/staf2131&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/staf2131&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.08768&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.08768&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
